---
// UX audits and talks, taken from Remi's own review and lecture decks.
const { part } = Astro.props; // 'audit' | 'talks'
const works = [
  ['Balanced, symmetrical layout', 'Every secondary button sits at the edge of the screen, which leaves the action button front and centre and shows the player where to go next.'],
  ['Easy flow', 'The main icons stay along the bottom on every screen. Nothing jumps around, and a new screen scrolls once by itself to show that it can.'],
  ['Hierarchy through scale and colour', 'Header, player info, chests, secondary buttons and the action button each read at their own level.'],
  ['Buttons where players expect them', 'Close and Back keep the positions players already know.'],
  ['Consistent UI art', 'Buttons are distinct by shape, size and style for each level of the hierarchy.'],
  ['Polish', 'Feedback on everything: animation, gleams and response to touch.'],
  ['A tutorial that shows, not tells', 'Simple, clear and quick. It never feels like work.'],
];
const risks = [
  ['Room to grow', 'The navigation is limited to five features. Adding a sixth will force a structural decision.'],
  ['Popups over popups', 'Usually a mistake. Here it is one level deep, a confirmation, and always returns to the previous screen, so it holds.'],
  ['Colour coding collision', 'The level droplet uses the same colour as epic cards, which muddies what that colour means.'],
];
const others = [
  { tag: 'Mobile strategy game · UX review', title: 'Strong systems, text too small.', points: ['Edge-to-edge UI keeps the centre clear and scales across devices', 'Tutorial is long and text-heavy; popups and info bubbles are hard to read', 'The call to action is unclear: which mode is the main game?', 'Recommendation: larger type, one clear primary action, cleaner UI art'] },
  { tag: 'Behaviour Interactive · UX solution', title: 'Make one mode the front door.', points: ['Brief: introduce a betting mode as the main funnel and de-emphasise the rest', 'Option one: a mode bar along the bottom with a dedicated mode-select screen', 'Option two: a single landing page where the new mode wins on size and colour', 'Delivered as wireframes and renders for both options'] },
];
const principles = ['The experience belongs to the user', 'UX is holistic', 'Great user experience is invisible', 'UX is a life cycle', 'Context', 'User-controlled experience', 'UX is social interaction', 'The psychological edge will win', 'UX is a conversation', 'Simplicity over complication'];
const venues = ['Hothead Games', 'Frima Studio', 'Bandai Namco', 'Behaviour Interactive', 'AppLovin'];
---
{part === 'audit' && <section class="section container" id="audit"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">UX audit · sample</p><h2>What an audit<br>actually says.</h2></div><p>An audit is the fastest way to start. This is the shape of one: Remi’s review of Clash Royale’s interface, written as a teaching example of what a strong mobile UI gets right and where it will strain.</p></div>
  <div class="in-audit sv-reveal">
    <div class="in-col good"><h3><span>7</span> things that work</h3><ol>{works.map(([title, body]) => <li><strong>{title}</strong><p>{body}</p></li>)}</ol></div>
    <div class="in-col risk"><h3><span>3</span> potential problems</h3><ol>{risks.map(([title, body]) => <li><strong>{title}</strong><p>{body}</p></li>)}</ol>
      <div class="in-get"><p class="in-kicker">What you receive</p><ul><li>Annotated screens and recordings</li><li>What works, and why to keep it</li><li>Problems ranked by impact and cost</li><li>A recommended next scope</li></ul><a class="button" href="/contact/?engagement=review#enquiry" data-track="cta_click" data-track-location="services_audit">Book an audit <span>↗</span></a></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="in-more">{others.map(item => <article class="sv-reveal"><p class="in-kicker">{item.tag}</p><h3>{item.title}</h3><ul>{item.points.map(point => <li>{point}</li>)}</ul></article>)}</div>
  <p class="sv-work-foot">Clash Royale is a trademark of Supercell. The review is independent commentary and was not commissioned.</p>
</section>}

{part === 'talks' && <section class="section container" id="talks"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Talks &amp; teaching</p><h2>Stop designing in screens.<br>Start designing in flow.</h2></div><p>The line Remi’s UX talk is built around. He has taught game interface design at Vancouver Film School and written this talk for the studios he has worked with.</p></div>
  <div class="in-talks sv-reveal">
    <div class="in-principles"><p class="in-kicker">10 principles of UX</p><ol>{principles.map(text => <li>{text}</li>)}</ol></div>
    <div class="in-side">
      <article><p class="in-kicker">The talk</p><h3>UX is not UI.</h3><p>Flow is the big picture; screens are the small detail. Design the player’s path first and the screens stop surprising you with features nobody planned for.</p><p class="in-venues">Versions written for {venues.slice(0, -1).join(', ')} and {venues[venues.length - 1]}.</p></article>
      <article><p class="in-kicker">Teaching</p><h3>Game Interface Design, VFS.</h3><p>Instructor at Vancouver Film School in 2016: wireframes, user flows, prototyping and usability for students entering game UI.</p></article>
      <article><p class="in-kicker">For your team</p><h3>A workshop, not a lecture.</h3><p>The same material runs as a half-day session with your designers and engineers, using your own game as the example.</p><a class="pf-link" href="/contact/?engagement=review#enquiry">Ask about a workshop →</a></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>}

<style is:global>
  .in-audit{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.35fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:24px;align-items:start}
  .in-col{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:18px;background:var(--surface);padding:34px 36px}
  .in-col h3{display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:14px;font-size:24px;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin-bottom:8px}
  .in-col h3 span{font:600 54px/1 Manrope,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.06em}
  .in-col.good h3 span{color:var(--accent)}.in-col.risk h3 span{color:#ff8a6b}
  .in-col ol{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;counter-reset:n}
  .in-col li{counter-increment:n;position:relative;padding:18px 0 18px 44px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
  .in-col li::before{content:counter(n,decimal-leading-zero);position:absolute;left:0;top:21px;font:500 11px/1 var(--mono);color:var(--muted)}
  .in-col li strong{font:600 17px/1.3 Manrope,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:var(--ink)}
  .in-col li p{font-size:14px;line-height:1.65;margin-top:6px}
  .in-kicker{font:500 10.5px/1.4 var(--mono);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--accent)}
  .in-get{margin-top:14px;padding:24px;border-radius:14px;background:linear-gradient(140deg,rgba(198,242,122,.1),transparent 60%),var(--surface-2);border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,var(--accent) 35%,transparent)}
  .in-get ul{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:14px 0 20px;display:grid;gap:8px;font-size:14px;color:var(--ink)}
  .in-get li{padding:0!important;border:0!important;display:flex;gap:10px}.in-get li::before{content:'✓'!important;position:static!important;color:var(--accent)!important;font:700 14px/1.4 inherit!important}
  .in-more{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:24px;margin-top:24px}
  .in-more article{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:16px;padding:30px 32px;background:var(--surface)}
  .in-more h3{font-size:25px;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:14px 0 16px}
  .in-more ul{padding-left:18px;margin:0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.9;color:var(--muted)}
  .in-talks{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1.15fr);gap:24px}
  .in-principles{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:18px;padding:34px 36px;background:var(--surface)}
  .in-principles ol{list-style:none;margin:16px 0 0;padding:0;counter-reset:p}
  .in-principles li{counter-increment:p;display:flex;gap:18px;align-items:baseline;padding:13px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);font:600 clamp(17px,1.5vw,21px)/1.3 Manrope,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.03em;color:var(--ink);transition:padding .25s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1),color .2s}
  .in-principles li:hover{padding-left:10px;color:var(--accent)}
  .in-principles li::before{content:counter(p,decimal-leading-zero);font:500 11px/1 var(--mono);color:var(--accent);letter-spacing:.06em}
  .in-side{display:grid;gap:16px}
  .in-side article{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:16px;padding:26px 28px;background:var(--surface)}
  .in-side h3{font-size:23px;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:12px 0 10px}
  .in-side p:not(.in-kicker){font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7}
  .in-venues{font:400 12px/1.7 var(--mono)!important;color:var(--muted);margin-top:12px}
  .in-side .pf-link{display:inline-block;margin-top:12px;font-size:14px;color:var(--accent);font-weight:600}
  @media(max-width:900px){.in-audit,.in-more,.in-talks{grid-template-columns:1fr}.in-col,.in-principles{padding:24px 22px}}
</style>
